<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mixe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ayuuk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mixe, who call themselves Ayuuk, are an Indigenous people of the mountains of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oaxaca">Oaxaca</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, speaking a language of the Mixe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoque">Zoque</a> family. From their rugged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> around Zempoaltépetl they resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zapotecs">Zapotecs</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a> and were only slowly brought under Spanish rule. They number more than 100,000 today and keep a strong tradition of community self-government.</p></div>
